ANSWER
  Routes (1), (2) and Fig. 9 reading B give r = 0.06, 0.40 (0.22-0.98), 0.49: below 1,
  so 50/50 is stable at every feed and arm G follows a seed to a bounded plateau.
  Fig. 9 reading A gives r = 1.14 (per point 1.06-1.23): inside the window, with
  m* = 10.1 mM feed, i.e. an R9 candidate.
  The paper's own data do not decide between them: it does not say which gel bands Fig. 9 counted.
  Decisive and cheap: the hand of the +1 nucleotide in Fig. 9's racemic lane (EXPERIMENT.md, Arm G step 0).

